"e":"che","d":"2019-10-30","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"David P. Williams","x":"…to conservatively we estimate it with a slightly more than 6% increase in Medicare reimbursement, we anticipate our Cap going from our roughly $9 million to $18 million for the run rate, which of course we'll dial down as we turn around and rightsize the mix of our admissions in various programs.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/10/30/chemed-corp-che-q3-2019-earnings-call-transcript.aspx"},{"c":"CHE 2019 Q4","e":"che","d":"2020-02-19","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Kevin J. McNamara","x":"This was driven by a combination of our 6.1% growth in average daily census, as well as our annual Medicare price increase that was effective October 1, 2019.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/02/19/chemed-corp-che-q4-2019-earnings-call-transcript.aspx"},{"c":"CHE 2019 Q4","e":"che","d":"2020-02-19","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"David P. Williams","x":"So the -- of course, we knew where we're going to get a price increase that was significantly higher than anyone anticipated when the CMS announced it in July, August and basically they were taking a rough cut of 20 basis points out of routine home care and then general inpatient care on a…","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/02/19/chemed-corp-che-q4-2019-earnings-call-transcript.aspx"},{"c":"CHE 2020 Q1","e":"che","d":"2020-04-29","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"David P. Williams","x":"The combination of a decline in Medicare Cap, increase in Medicaid net room and board pass through and other contra revenue activity had minimal impact on overall revenue growth in the quarter.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/04/29/chemed-corp-che-q1-2020-earnings-call-transcript.aspx"},{"c":"CHE 2020 Q2","e":"che","d":"2020-07-30","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"David P. Williams","x":"…phase of our projected operating results, we would then modify the projections for the timing of price increases, changing the commission structure, wages, marketing programs and a variety of continuous improvement initiatives that our business segments plan on executing over the coming year.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/07/30/chemed-corp-che-q2-2020-earnings-call-transcript.aspx"},{"c":"CHE 2020 Q2","e":"che","d":"2020-07-30","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Kevin J. McNamara","x":"We made the decision for Roto-Rooter to maintain full staffing and operating capacity with no employee layoffs, as we entered the second quarter.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/07/30/chemed-corp-che-q2-2020-earnings-call-transcript.aspx"},{"c":"CHE 2020 Q2","e":"che","d":"2020-07-30","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Nick Westfall","x":"Related to head count management supporting our people and like, Roto-Rooter, we have not furloughed or laid off a single employee throughout this pandemic.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/07/30/chemed-corp-che-q2-2020-earnings-call-transcript.aspx"},{"c":"CHE 2020 Q3","e":"che","d":"2020-10-30","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Kevin J. McNamara","x":"That's -- when we raised guidance for the fourth quarter, a driving factor in that is Roto-Rooter.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/10/30/chemed-corp-che-q3-2020-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"CHE 2020 Q3","e":"che","d":"2020-10-30","l":"guidance","r":"analyst","s":"Joanna Gajuk","x":"So how should we think about -- and obviously, you raised guidance, so I guess you're expecting this to be reflective in Q4 as well, but how should we think about next year's margins?","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/10/30/chemed-corp-che-q3-2020-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"CHE 2020 Q4","e":"che","d":"2021-02-24","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"David P. Williams","x":"The combination of